* Multi-ring-oscillator XOR entropy source: three free-running CMOS ring
* oscillators of different stage counts (so their nominal frequencies
* differ, per the entry's own layout idiom), combined by a 2-stage XOR tree
* and sampled by a slow reference strobe through the same transmission-gate
* sampling latch ring-oscillator-jitter-trng uses.
* sky130 schematic-level netlist BODY -- no .control/.end (klt sim wraps this).
* Device W/L are in microns (sky130_fd_pr subckt convention).
*
* Authored from kb/entries/multi-ro-xor-entropy-source.json's own topology/
* sizing_approach text, not imported from anywhere (kb/SOURCING.md):
*
*   "N independent free-running ring oscillators whose outputs are combined
*    by a single XOR tree ... and then sampled by a slow reference clock.
*    Each ring contributes independent phase jitter; XOR-ing many nominally
*    independent jittery edges accumulates their entropy..."
*
*   "physically separate the N rings and vary their stage counts/
*    orientations so they do not injection-lock into a common frequency"
*
* N=3 HERE, NOT A LARGER N. The entry leaves N general ("N independent...
* rings"); three is the smallest N that actually exercises a "tree" (two
* XOR2 gates, not one) while keeping the netlist a from-scratch reference
* rather than an arbitrarily large array. Stage counts 5/7/9 are chosen
* specifically so their free-running periods are mutually incommensurate
* (no small-integer ratio between any pair), directly implementing the
* "vary their stage counts... so they do not injection-lock" layout idiom
* above at the schematic level (this testbench has no substrate/supply
* coupling model, so "injection-lock" isn't literally at risk here -- the
* frequency SPACING is what the incommensurate stage counts buy).
*
* WHAT THIS TESTBENCH CAN AND CANNOT SHOW -- same disclosure as
* ring-oscillator-jitter-trng's netlist header, restated for N=3: ngspice's
* transient analysis is deterministic (no thermal noise to accumulate), so
* this testbench cannot demonstrate real accumulated entropy or an actual
* min-entropy improvement from XOR-combining N=3 independent noise sources
* over N=1. What it verifies is the SENSITIVITY/COMBINING MECHANISM: each
* ring's own free-running frequency (f_ring5_hz/f_ring7_hz/f_ring9_hz below)
* is distinct, and the XOR-combined, strobed output is not a constant bit
* across samples -- the deterministic skeleton real (noise-driven) jitter
* would ride on top of to become unpredictable. See
* ring-oscillator-jitter-trng's header for the single-ring baseline this
* entry's own notes say it generalizes.
*
* THE SAMPLER IS A TRANSPARENT LATCH WITH A NARROW ENABLE WINDOW, same
* simplification (and same rationale) as ring-oscillator-jitter-trng's.
*
* THE XOR TREE IS BUILT FROM TRANSMISSION-GATE 2:1 MULTIPLEXERS, THE
* SMALLEST STANDARD CMOS XOR2 CONSTRUCTION: XOR2(a,b) = a ? b : NOT(b),
* implemented as one inverter (b -> b_bar) feeding two complementary
* transmission gates gated by a/a_bar, tied together at the output. Two
* XOR2 stages combine three rings: xor_ab = ring5 XOR ring7;
* xor_out = xor_ab XOR ring9. No output buffering between XOR2 stages --
* a real implementation would buffer a TG-mux output before using it as
* another gate's select input; skipped here because a MOSFET gate draws no
* DC current, so the unbuffered node still settles to a valid logic level
* between ring transitions, at the cost of using a slightly slower-settling
* signal to drive the second XOR2's controls than a real design would want.
*
* Node map:
*   r1_5..r5_5    -- 5-stage ring ("ring5") stage outputs
*   r1_7..r7_7    -- 7-stage ring ("ring7") stage outputs
*   r1_9..r9_9    -- 9-stage ring ("ring9") stage outputs
*   xor_ab        -- ring5 XOR ring7 (first XOR2 stage's output)
*   xor_out       -- xor_ab XOR ring9 (combined entropy source output)
*   smp/smp_b     -- slow reference strobe and its complement
*   samp, y_b, y  -- sampler internal/held nodes; y is the sampled output
*
* SIZING
*   All three rings: the same plain (unstarved) CMOS inverter stage as
*   ring-oscillator-jitter-trng's (wn=1/wp=2/L=0.15, 50fF per-stage load).
*   Measured free-running frequencies: f_ring5_hz/f_ring7_hz/f_ring9_hz
*   below (ring5 matches ring-oscillator-jitter-trng's single ring exactly).
*   XOR2 transmission gates: wtg=1/L=0.15, the same drive strength as the
*   sampler's own pass gate.
*   Sampler: identical construction and sizing to
*   ring-oscillator-jitter-trng's (see that netlist's header for the
*   pass-gate/hold-inverter/weak-feedback-keeper sizing rationale).
.param wn=1 wp=2 l=0.15 cload=50f
.param wtg=1 wtgfb=1 ltg=0.15 ltgfb=1.0

Vdd vdd 0 DC 1.8

* --- ring5 (5-stage) ---
XIP1_5 r1_5 r5_5 vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 L={l} W={wp} nf=1 mult=1
XIN1_5 r1_5 r5_5 0   0   sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L={l} W={wn} nf=1 mult=1
C1_5 r1_5 0 {cload}
XIP2_5 r2_5 r1_5 vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 L={l} W={wp} nf=1 mult=1
XIN2_5 r2_5 r1_5 0   0   sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L={l} W={wn} nf=1 mult=1
C2_5 r2_5 0 {cload}
XIP3_5 r3_5 r2_5 vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 L={l} W={wp} nf=1 mult=1
XIN3_5 r3_5 r2_5 0   0   sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L={l} W={wn} nf=1 mult=1
C3_5 r3_5 0 {cload}
XIP4_5 r4_5 r3_5 vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 L={l} W={wp} nf=1 mult=1
XIN4_5 r4_5 r3_5 0   0   sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L={l} W={wn} nf=1 mult=1
C4_5 r4_5 0 {cload}
XIP5_5 r5_5 r4_5 vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 L={l} W={wp} nf=1 mult=1
XIN5_5 r5_5 r4_5 0   0   sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 L={l} W={wn} nf=1 mult=1
C5_5 r5_5 0 {cload}

